Yes!

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:30.540
So beautiful!

00:16:30.580 --> 00:16:31.950
It's a Drop.

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:33.080
Huh?

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:37.700
That iDOL from before destroyed a Drop
that's burning up in the atmosphere.

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:39.750
You don't get to see that very often.

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:45.540
It's incredible. It's been a while since
I've seen the ocean, too.

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:46.790
Is that so?

00:16:46.790 --> 00:16:49.120
My hometown doesn't have an ocean.

00:16:49.660 --> 00:16:57.000
It's like sparkling rain... A long time ago,
the konpeito was a single large clump, huh?

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:58.910
They called it the Moon, right?

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:02.450
I wonder if the ocean was this
beautiful back then, too.

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:08.040
Who knows? But I'm sure no scenery
could be more beautiful than this.

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:09.120
I know, right?!

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:12.250
What's wrong?

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:13.580
It's glowing again.

00:17:13.910 --> 00:17:15.290
"Again"?

00:17:15.290 --> 00:17:18.160
This is the third time since I've come here.

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:21.250
That hasn't happened with me at all.

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:22.660
I wonder what's going on...

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:27.160
Still, showing us something
as beautiful as all that...

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:29.500
Those "iDOLs" are pretty cool, huh?

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:32.330
Pretty cool, huh?

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:40.540
That's a wrap.

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:42.540
Good job.

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:45.200
Return path and recovery route is confirmed.

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:46.950
Makoto, good work.

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:48.910
Huh?

00:17:48.910 --> 00:17:50.040
What's wrong?

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:52.450
A reaction in Hangar No. 7?

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:57.790
No. 7? The Prometheus,
which has been sealed off for so long?

00:18:03.450 --> 00:18:05.620
Where... did you come from?

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:07.160
Let's play!

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:13.870
I never thought you'd come out here personally.

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:16.370
Working in the public sector
isn't all fun and games.

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:19.910
Output in Hangar No. 7 keeps increasing!

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:21.910
There is no outside interference.

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:25.000
So, this is output from Prometheus 1?

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:27.830
We're out of options.
Send an emergency signal to-

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:28.950
It's no good!

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:32.450
There's interference from
the konpeito and... This is...

00:18:32.620 --> 00:18:34.120
It's jamming!

00:18:35.160 --> 00:18:37.080
W-we should play?

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:38.000
Yeah!

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:41.370
Um, we're sort of lost right now, so...

00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:42.870
I know.

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:46.750
I know where you want to go, too.

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:48.540
But that's...

00:18:48.580 --> 00:18:49.830
You know what?

00:18:49.910 --> 00:18:51.870
You're coming with me!

00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:56.910
Haruka!

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:09.160
Seismic gravity confirmed in Hangar No. 7!

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:11.790
The bulkhead is stripping off the inner wall!

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:14.370
It's trying to get to the surface?!

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:21.330
What's that?!

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:35.950
Haruka!

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:40.160
What?

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:42.500
This is...

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:47.580
It can't be!

00:19:52.700 --> 00:19:53.450
The Prometheus 1!

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:55.040
It's coming aboveground!

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:11.290
Impossible...

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:13.830
The Imber!

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:25.370
Wait, what's this?!

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:27.250
Hey, hold on!

00:20:27.250 --> 00:20:29.200
What am I supposed to do?!

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:45.620
Imber!

00:20:45.790 --> 00:20:47.910
Hey, now what?!

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:08.080
Wh-what?

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:14.700
What? What is this?!

00:21:15.410 --> 00:21:17.250
Chihaya! What do we do?

00:21:17.660 --> 00:21:20.330
Prometheus 1's gravity field has disappeared.

00:21:21.160 --> 00:21:23.250
Picking up new readings by the seashore.

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:26.450
It's Prometheus 3, the Nubilum!

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:31.410
Chihaya!

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:33.040
You follow me!

00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:34.540
Come on!

00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:41.450
The Nubilum!

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:51.870
Izayoi
Dorm

00:21:54.540 --> 00:22:03.500
Like a saint that crosses the ages

00:22:03.500 --> 00:22:12.450
In what kind of loneliness did you cry?

00:22:12.450 --> 00:22:21.330
Stretching out to a star so far away

00:22:21.330 --> 00:22:29.870
Say, I'll depict my feelings, look up at the sky

00:22:31.500 --> 00:22:41.330
Dear boy, if I always look for you in my heart

00:22:41.330 --> 00:22:50.290
Ah, I'll release a light so strong it will envelop you

00:22:50.290 --> 00:22:59.250
That sparkling trail will be the guide for us both

00:22:59.250 --> 00:23:26.080
Now, no matter where we look, we feel the truth

00:23:26.080 --> 00:23:41.080
Preview
An iDOL Master

00:23:26.660 --> 00:23:28.950
Yayoi, what should we do for the preview?

00:23:28.950 --> 00:23:30.700
You should just do a simple summary.

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:32.000
Okay, describe today's story in one word.

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:33.200
Um, shrimp?

00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:34.700
What about next time, in one word?

00:23:34.700 --> 00:23:36.200
Um, anthocyanin?

00:23:36.200 --> 00:23:38.830
There you have it.
Next episode is about anthocyanin.

00:23:38.830 --> 00:23:40.000
Is that really okay?
